Template: pii-guard-proxy/modes
Type: multiselect
Choices: claude-code, https-proxy, browser
Default: claude-code
Description: Select the proxy mode(s) to activate
 PII Guard can route different kinds of traffic through itself. Pick one or
 more — they all share the same anonymization map, so values stay consistent
 between Claude Code, your CLI tools, and your browser.
 .
 claude-code: write /etc/profile.d/pii-guard-claude-code.sh which exports
  ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8765 system-wide. Routes Claude Code
  and any Anthropic SDK app through the proxy on next shell login.
 .
 https-proxy: write /etc/profile.d/pii-guard-https-proxy.sh which exports
  HTTPS_PROXY, HTTP_PROXY and NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS system-wide. Routes any
  CLI/SDK that respects the standard proxy env vars (curl, OpenAI SDK,
  Gemini SDK, etc.) through the proxy.
 .
 browser: install a Chromium/Chrome managed-policy file pointing the
  browser at the proxy and disabling QUIC, plus add the CA to the
  installing user's NSS database. Chrome on this machine then routes
  through the proxy automatically with no flags or extensions.

Template: pii-guard-proxy/install-deps
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Install missing runtime packages (nodejs, libnss3-tools) automatically?
 The proxy needs Node.js >= 18 to run, and libnss3-tools (certutil) is
 required if you choose the browser mode. If either is missing, postinst
 will run apt-get to install them. Disable this only if you want to manage
 those packages yourself.

Template: pii-guard-proxy/browser-restart-warning
Type: note
Description: Open browsers will be closed when this install finishes
 You selected the "browser" mode. Chrome, Chromium, Brave, and Edge only
 read managed policy files at startup, so the installer will SIGTERM (and
 SIGKILL after 2 s) any running instances of those browsers. Their tabs
 will be restored when you reopen them.
 .
 Please save any unsaved work in those browsers before continuing.
